    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d237">

                <pb facs="0217" n="207" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg207"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">714.44A15/232: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Guatemala</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Des Portes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-03-18T17:00:00-05:00">March 18, 1941—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>43. Personal for the Under Secretary.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d237-f1"/> Upon my
                    return here I find a strongly revived interest among high Guatemalan officials
                    regarding Belize. It is evident that they have expected me to bring some
                    definite news regarding progress in the negotiations.</p>
                <p>From a statement made by the Under Secretary for Foreign Affairs it is clear that
                    President Ubico hopes to receive Belize outright in connection with the Lease
                    Lend Bill.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d237-f2"/></p>
                <p>This matter is certain to come up for discussion at an early date notably when I
                    call on the President. I should consequently appreciate any information which
                    you may permit me to communicate to the President and other appropriate
                    Guatemalan officials if only in order that they may not indulge in unwarrantedly
                    high hopes.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Des Portes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
